# the sse2 to sse4.2 sequences of the x86-64 table that the admission rule gains: rows with no one instruction,
# each correct for every input and made of instructions whose timing reads no lane's value
#
# bytes multiply through words and shift one bit of the count at a time, quadwords multiply through pmuludq and
# shift right arithmetically as the logical shift of the value flipped by its sign, an ordered comparison of
# quadwords below sse4.2 is a doubleword comparison of the high halves joined with an unsigned one of the low
# halves, and the conversions between doublewords and floats saturate
# as the scalar ones do. the rules are in the table's list.

